# Latest first

- Put each new update at the top of the relevant maintained README, report or result index, immediately after its title or current summary.
- Order dated entries newest first; a later update on the same date also goes above earlier entries.
- Distinguish prepared settings, offline verification and completed model results.
- Preserve frozen protocols, source snapshots and archived results byte for byte. Put new findings in a new record and link the older evidence.
